WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.340
Yeah, you guessed it: another day, another
provocative Marvel rumor.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.020
Citing their ever-mysterious inside sources,
We Got This Covered is now reporting that

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:14.269
Marvel Studios is considering DC leading light
Henry Cavill for the role of Captain Britain

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:15.820
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.560
Now, as usual, it should go without saying
that this rumor needs to be taken with a whole

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.540
shaker of salt.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.880
We Got This Covered don't exactly have the
best track record with Marvel news, and the

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:31.500
site's assertion that Cavill hasn't been contacted
about the role but is instead on a "wish list"

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.960
doesn't seem to mesh with Marvel's usual commitment
to total security.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.420
Having said all that, however, Marvel has
actually already planted the seeds for Captain

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.200
Britain's arrival in the MCU with a brief
line in Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.560
It's hard to hear but when you have the closed
captions on you can see that the name Braddock

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.060
get mentioned.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:52.520
Otherwise known as Brian Braddock, Captain
Britain first appeared in the pages of Marvel

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.360
comics all the way back in 1976.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.260
And although you might assume otherwise, Braddock
is anything but a simple British copy of Captain

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.140
America despite the two sharing similar names.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:08.540
A gifted young physicist, Braddock was working
on an experiment involving antimatter particles

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:13.360
when he had a fateful run-in with the supervillain
Reaver, who was intent on stealing the research

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.220
for himself.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.760
Braddock sustained what would have been fatal
injuries when he crashed his motorcycle while

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.750
fleeing the scene but he was rescued by Merlin,
who gifted him with the legendary Amulet of

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.240
Right.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:25.660
Yeah, that Merlin.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:30.280
In addition to saving his life, the Amulet
of Right granted Braddock superpowers on par

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.340
with the mightiest of Earth's mightiest heroes.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:38.520
He can fly, he's near-indestructible, he has
Daredevil-esque sharpened senses, and he can

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.000
even take on some of the Marvel universe's
most powerful heroes.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:46.980
The only real drawback to all this is that
his magically-imbued powers wane if he ventures

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.680
outside the U.K. unless he wears his special
super-suit, of course.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:56.520
Marvel die-hards have been fan casting Braddock
since at least 2017, when Kevin Feige name-dropped

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.300
the character as one that he'd like to explore
in the future.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:03.980
On the press tour for Spider-Man: Homecoming,
the producer was asked about whether the studio

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.900
had plans to introduce Captain Britain.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.120
We have discussed it.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:11.720
There are a lot of actors that come in and
ask about that part, so we'll have to see."

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:16.320
Of course, it's likely that fan castings are
the real source of the Cavill rumor, too.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:21.600
In September 2018, Twitter users raised the
possibility of Cavill playing Captain Britain

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.580
after it was reported that he had finished
playing Superman for Warner Brothers.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.280
Mostly, this flurry of scuttlebut was based
around the fact that Cavill is square-jawed,

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.060
British, and looks good in a superhero suit.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.760
And that should be enough, right?

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.220
But Cavill himself has done nothing whatsoever
to fuel these flames, and there are actually

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:42.110
a number of other British actors who have
expressed their own interest in playing the

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:42.600
role, too.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:47.540
One of these is Simon Pegg, who told JoBlo
in 2018 that he had loved the character when

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:50.840
he was a kid and even had his own Captain
Britain mask.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:55.440
Pegg has proven his action bonafides with
roles in the Star Trek and Mission: Impossible

00:02:55.459 --> 00:02:59.400
franchises over the last few years, but he
did mention at the time that he feared he

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.940
may be too old for a major superhero role.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:05.540
Considering he's currently 49 years old, that
seems to hold true.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:09.900
Another name that keeps popping up in relation
to Captain Britain is Orlando Bloom, who threw

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:13.980
his name into the conversation during an interview
at around the same time as Pegg.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:18.520
Heck, even Tom Hiddleston has expressed interest
in taking on the role, but that seems likely

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.160
to have been a joke, considering… well,
you know.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.160
“Surprise.”

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:27.480
It's also worth noting that, while it was
widely reported last year that Cavill had

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.660
split from Warner Brothers and DC, this break-up
has never actually been officially confirmed.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.840
In the wake of those reports, the studio issued
a statement saying that it has, quote, "a

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:41.769
great relationship and great respect" for
Cavill, and that "no current decisions regarding

00:03:41.769 --> 00:03:44.240
any upcoming Superman films" had been made.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:48.820
And while the franchise has been undergoing
an extensive recalibration as of late, it's

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:52.950
certainly not outside the realm of possibility
to think that Cavill could eventually return

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:54.160
to the role of Superman.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.440
All in all, this Cavill rumor appears to be
highly suspect, and there's honestly a good

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.040
chance that it's all a bunch of malarkey.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.340
Still, you never know.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:05.160
And either way, you're best keeping your eyes
peeled because Brian Braddock could still

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:09.280
be popping up in the MCU sometime soon, whether
Cavill takes the role or not.

